-- title:
--   Unit Uₚ-eigenvalue interpolated in the localised anemic Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field, let $p$ be an odd prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms, factoring through a finite level) whose base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p \in S$, let $N \geq 1$ have all its prime factors in $S$, assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by the lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansions, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q$ prime, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (i.e. $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Assume further $p \mid N$, $p^2 \nmid N$, and that $\bar\rho$, read as an adic representation over $k$, is ordinary at $p$: for each valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit there is a $k$-line $L$ spanned by a member of a basis of the representation space, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, with $\bar\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and all $v$. Then there exists $u$ in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisation of the Hecke algebra data at the submonoid attached to $\theta$) with the following property. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete and with finite residue field, which is a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra with local structure map, let $\psi$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to $\mathcal O'$, let $M \geq 1$ divide $N$, and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem does not already occur at any proper divisor of $M$). Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell) = a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient, for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S \setminus \{p\}$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$ matching $\psi$ on the away-from-$S$ Hecke operators, that is $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) = \psi(\pi(T_\ell))$ for all primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, where $\pi$ is the structure map to the localisation. Then: if $p \mid M$, there is $a \in \{1,-1\}$ with $a_p(g) = a$ in $\mathbb C$ and $\psi(u) = a$ in $\mathcal O'$; and if $p \nmid M$ and $\iota(\chi_g(T_p))$ is a unit of $\mathcal O'$, then $\psi(u)$ is a unit and $\psi(u)^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_p))\,\psi(u) + p = 0$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic half of the assertion that $U_p$ is redundant in the $\theta$-localised anemic Hecke algebra when $p$ exactly divides the level and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$: the element $u$ interpolates, at each congruent newform of level $M \mid N$, the sign $a_p(g) = \pm 1$ when $p \mid M$ and the unit root of $X^2 - a_p(g)X + p$ when $p \nmid M$. Nothing is asserted at newforms of level prime to $p$ whose $p$-th Hecke eigenvalue fails to be a unit. It is used in the identification of $U_p$ with an anemic Hecke operator in the localised algebra and in the construction of the associated residual unit-root data.
